he particle at time $t=5?$" 13194139534882 false] [17592186313641 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/assets/18904539463b95f9d681f61f0d8f875ad0cb03b35d4037e75c227d4523502193.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the velocity of an object moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis. At time $t=1$ the particle is located at the position $x=2.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=5?$" 13194139534882 true] [17592186313655 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/assets/1df00f421b20b101d1500b4e2f47054f0c79dcfd2d82585fb8fb3735adb71af5.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the velocity of an object moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis. At time $t=2$ the particle is located at the position $x=5.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=9?$" 13194139534882 false] [17592186313655 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/assets/1df00f421b20b101d1500b4e2f47054f0c79dcfd2d82585fb8fb3735adb71af5.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the velocity of an object moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis. At time $t=2$ the particle is located at the position $x=5.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=9?$" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317099 1017 #edb/ref 17592186317100 13194139534882 true] [17592186317099 1089 "q-2417" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317099 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534882 true] [17592186317099 1100 "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t>0$ is given by $v(t)=6{t}^{2}+4t.$ At time $t=4$ the particle is located at the position $x=-300.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=7?$" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317099 1113 #uuid "5831fc2e-764d-5a31-8755-1f580d3a4978" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317099 1145 "The position of the particle at $t=7$ is equal to its position at $t=4$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [4,7].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(7)=x(4)+{\\int }_{4}^{7}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nCarrying out the computations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(7) & =-300+{\\int }_{4}^{7}(6{t}^{2}+4t)\\,\\text{dt} \\\\  & =-300+{[2{t}^{3}+2{t}^{2})]}_{4}^{7} \\\\  & =-300+([2(7)^{3}+2(7)^{2}]-[2(4)^{3}+2(4)^{2}]) \\\\  & =-300+([686+98]-[128+32]) \\\\  & =-300+(784-160) \\\\  & =-300+624 \\\\  & =324.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=7$ is $x=324.$" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317100 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317101 13194139534882 true] [17592186317100 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317102 13194139534882 true] [17592186317100 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317103 13194139534882 true] [17592186317100 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317104 13194139534882 true] [17592186317100 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317105 13194139534882 true] [17592186317100 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534882 true] [17592186317100 1041 "selection" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317100 1104 #edb/ref 17592186317101 13194139534882 true] [17592186317100 1110 #uuid "792b11c7-7227-5f02-917b-c8e6000176a0" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317101 1034 "324" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317101 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534882 true] [17592186317101 1111 #uuid "f40f1b33-c29b-5929-91ff-0f0a7d405bef" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317102 1034 "453" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317102 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534882 true] [17592186317102 1111 #uuid "5e502939-66a9-58f2-8483-22e61f79f86f" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317103 1034 "269" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317103 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534882 true] [17592186317103 1111 #uuid "8cfdc686-2da9-542f-8416-945c31df98ba" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317104 1034 "214" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317104 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534882 true] [17592186317104 1111 #uuid "a85a23e7-ec63-5eb1-addb-0f450089f786" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317105 1034 "221" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317105 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534882 true] [17592186317105 1111 #uuid "3e685537-fdec-5193-b919-f201a7bd1e10" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317106 1017 #edb/ref 17592186317107 13194139534882 true] [17592186317106 1089 "q-348281" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317106 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534882 true] [17592186317106 1100 "A particle $Q$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t$ is given by $v(t)=6{t}^{2}-4t.$ Find the total displacement $d$ of the particle between $t=0$ and $t=5.$\n\n$d=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317106 1113 #uuid "1352850d-196b-5e3b-b4aa-7a3aa8b03b2c" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317106 1145 "We find the total displacement by calculating the definite integral of the velocity.\n\nLet $d$ be the total displacement between $t=0$ and $t=5.$ Then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={\\int }_{0}^{5}(6{t}^{2}-4t)\\,\\text{dt} \\\\  & =(2{t}^{3}-2{t}^{2}){|}_{0}^{5} \\\\  & =[2(5)^{3}-2(5)^{2}]-[2(0)^{3}-2(0)^{2}] \\\\  & =[250-50]-0 \\\\  & =200.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317107 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317108 13194139534882 true] [17592186317107 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534882 true] [17592186317107 1041 "field-1" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317107 1104 #edb/ref 17592186317108 13194139534882 true] [17592186317107 1110 #uuid "8665b4bb-f5ff-5512-a0aa-62e8272667c0" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317108 1034 "200" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317108 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534882 true] [17592186317108 1111 #uuid "6ed8794f-8d5f-5151-a373-508d49d28475" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317109 1017 #edb/ref 17592186317110 13194139534882 true] [17592186317109 1089 "q-351420" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317109 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534882 true] [17592186317109 1100 "A particle $Q$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t$ is given by $v(t)=-4t-1.$ Find the total displacement $d$ of the particle between $t=0$ and $t=1.$\n\n$d=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317109 1113 #uuid "26d9513e-8557-587b-a7aa-f43d97b00bb3" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317109 1145 "We find the total displacement by calculating the definite integral of the velocity.\n\nLet $d$ be the total displacement between $t=0$ and $t=1.$ Then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(-4t-1)\\,\\text{dt} \\\\  & =(-2{t}^{2}-t){|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =[-2(1)^{2}-(1)]-[-2(0)^{2}-(0)] \\\\  & =[-2-1]-0 \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317110 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317111 13194139534882 true] [17592186317110 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317112 13194139534882 true] [17592186317110 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534882 true] [17592186317110 1041 "field-1" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317110 1104 #edb/ref 17592186317112 13194139534882 true] [17592186317110 1110 #uuid "92f08796-c227-5008-9923-4794a926e496" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317111 1034 "3" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317111 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534882 true] [17592186317111 1111 #uuid "c7b0ee78-9caa-591c-bf3e-ae677d383656" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317112 1034 "-3" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317112 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534882 true] [17592186317112 1111 #uuid "30558b2d-f9d9-5a82-8400-bc8e75e57f74" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317113 1017 #edb/ref 17592186317114 13194139534882 true] [17592186317113 1089 "q-351442" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317113 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534882 true] [17592186317113 1100 "A particle $Q$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t$ is given by $v(t)=\\frac{1}{1+{t}^{2}}.$ Find the total displacement $d$ of the particle between $t=0$ and $t=1.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$d=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317113 1113 #uuid "97403b47-5240-5854-b79c-59d3da5d4bb0" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317113 1145 "We find the total displacement by calculating the definite integral of the velocity.\n\nLet $d$ be the total displacement between $t=0$ and $t=1.$ Then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{1}{1+{t}^{2}})\\,\\text{dt} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(t)){|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1)-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317114 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317115 13194139534882 true] [17592186317114 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317116 13194139534882 true] [17592186317114 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534882 true] [17592186317114 1041 "field-1" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317114 1104 #edb/ref 17592186317115 13194139534882 true] [17592186317114 1110 #uuid "9038322d-cc66-50ab-a7ab-1cfda5851b5d" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317115 1034 "\\frac{\\pi}{4}" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317115 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534882 true] [17592186317115 1111 #uuid "499aacff-594b-5c11-a8e2-162bbfe14224" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317116 1034 "1" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317116 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534882 true] [17592186317116 1111 #uuid "d465bbe6-3dbd-5530-8b0c-417c00332fc9" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317117 1017 #edb/ref 17592186317118 13194139534882 true] [17592186317117 1089 "q-351448" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317117 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534882 true] [17592186317117 1100 "A particle $Q$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t\\ge 0$ is given by $v(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t).$ At time $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ the particle is located at the position $x=5.$ \nFind the position of the particle at time $t=\\pi .$ Do not round the answer.\n\nThe position of the particle at $t=\\pi $ is $x=$\n{{field-1}}." 13194139534882 true] [17592186317117 1113 #uuid "a6304d94-83b6-5e47-99ea-2a324e57b572" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317117 1145 "The position of the particle at $t=\\pi $ is equal to its position at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pi ].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(\\pi )=x(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nCarrying out the computations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(\\pi ) & =5+{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t))\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =5+{[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)]}_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =5+[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )]-[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})) \\\\  & =5+(0-1)-(1+0) \\\\  & =5-2 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the position of the particle at $t=\\pi $ is $x=3.$" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317118 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317119 13194139534882 true] [17592186317118 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534882 true] [17592186317118 1041 "field-1" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317118 1104 #edb/ref 17592186317119 13194139534882 true] [17592186317118 1110 #uuid "56912d8e-2282-50a1-b8f1-7c273bbfe54b" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317119 1034 "3" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317119 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534882 true] [17592186317119 1111 #uuid "45a04164-bff4-56a7-8f76-8a4c21319410" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317120 1017 #edb/ref 17592186317121 13194139534882 true] [17592186317120 1089 "q-351472" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317120 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534882 true] [17592186317120 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/assets/a3fb5a3a6102485294de519cc1372b7a348235317336a1d4c7fdbcf88be019b2.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the velocity of an object moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis. At time $t=3,$ the particle is located at the position $x=3.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=7?$\n\nThe position of the particle at $t=7$ is $x=$\n{{field-1}}." 13194139534882 true] [17592186317120 1113 #uuid "cef565e7-787d-578b-a8be-b1fe99f0a51c" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317120 1145 "The position of the particle at $t=7$ is equal to its position at $t=3$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [3,7].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(7)=x(3)+{\\int }_{3}^{7}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nWe are told that $x(3)=3$, and we can compute the integral ${\\int }_{3}^{7}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ by finding the signed area under the graph from $t=3$ to $t=7.$ Computing the signed area, we get\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{3}^{7}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t=8.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nx(7)=3+8=11.\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=7$ is $x=11.$" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317121 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317122 13194139534882 true] [17592186317121 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534882 true] [17592186317121 1041 "field-1" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317121 1104 #edb/ref 17592186317122 13194139534882 true] [17592186317121 1110 #uuid "646bf74a-2efd-599c-84e7-ef18756f9212" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317122 1034 "11" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317122 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534882 true] [17592186317122 1111 #uuid "d3d6a6f4-5207-5d1e-b17c-8fdb9cb76df7" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317123 1017 #edb/ref 17592186317124 13194139534882 true] [17592186317123 1089 "q-84265" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317123 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534882 true] [17592186317123 1100 "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t>0$ is given by $v(t)={e}^{t-1}.$ At time $t=1$ the particle is located at the position $x=2.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=2?$" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317123 1113 #uuid "301e0eb4-35d3-5c4c-920a-0903dcd0b3ba" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317123 1145 "The position of the particle at $t=2$ is equal to its position at $t=1$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [1,2].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(2)=x(1)+{\\int }_{1}^{2}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nCarrying out the computations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(2) & =2+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{e}^{t-1}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2+{[{e}^{t-1}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =2+({e}^{2-1}-{e}^{1-1}) \\\\  & =2+({e}^{1}-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =2+e-1 \\\\  & =e+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=2$ is $x=e+1.$" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317124 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317125 13194139534882 true] [17592186317124 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317126 13194139534882 true] [17592186317124 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317127 13194139534882 true] [17592186317124 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317128 13194139534882 true] [17592186317124 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317129 13194139534882 true] [17592186317124 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534882 true] [17592186317124 1041 "selection" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317124 1104 #edb/ref 17592186317127 13194139534882 true] [17592186317124 1110 #uuid "b8f4b06a-af27-5068-b635-d916b5e1842c" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317125 1034 "e+2" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317125 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534882 true] [17592186317125 1111 #uuid "de45d70e-3a87-5e14-908f-e023cfbc45d1" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317126 1034 "2e" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317126 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534882 true] [17592186317126 1111 #uuid "bf28dac6-5262-5ef8-ae61-260c80d0852a" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317127 1034 "e+1" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317127 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534882 true] [17592186317127 1111 #uuid "0116b71d-c4f0-5ff8-b474-601f05d618d6" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317128 1034 "e" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317128 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534882 true] [17592186317128 1111 #uuid "af1f8aef-223b-5f91-b856-ac95f42bf92c" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317129 1034 "2e+1" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317129 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534882 true] [17592186317129 1111 #uuid "d2213493-201f-5d6c-8c92-575820b9fe79" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317130 1017 #edb/ref 17592186317131 13194139534882 true] [17592186317130 1089 "q-84315" 13194139534882 true] [17592186317130 1091 #edb/ref 1759218